        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હલવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હલવું — halvũ — \"to shake; to move\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાત્રે અચાનક ધરતી હલી. rātre acānak dhartī halī. Suddenly in the night the ground shook."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): તે મકાન હલ્યું, te makān halyũ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હલવું (halvũ) comes from hallati, \"moves, shakes\", a form CDIAL reconstructs, where it lists Gujarati hālvũ, \"to move, shake\" (CDIAL 14018). હલાવવું, to stir, is its causative: you shake a thing, but the ground હલે છે by itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
